@baseUrl = http://localhost:4002
@accessToken = replace-with-a-token-whose-role-has-inbox.manage
@threadId = replace-with-an-id-from-a-list

### The channels this role may open, and whether each is connected. 403 without inbox.manage
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inbox/channels
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Visitor conversations, open ones first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inbox/messages?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### The same list, matching a keyword against one field of the item. An unknown field is 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inbox/messages?field=contact&keyword=sam@example.com
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### GitHub issues. 403 without github.manage, 502 while no repository is connected
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inbox/github?keyword=checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Closed member conversations. 403 without conversations.manage
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inbox/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### A channel that is not plugged in: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inbox/unknown
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### One thread with its messages and what staff may do to it
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inbox/messages/{{threadId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Reply (201). 409 once resolved, 400 on a channel that takes no replies
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/inbox/messages/{{threadId}}/replies
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"body":"Thanks for getting in touch. Here is the pricing page."}

### Resolve (204). On the GitHub channel this closes the issue
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/inbox/messages/{{threadId}}/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Delete the thread and everything in it (204). 400 on a channel that cannot delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/inbox/messages/{{threadId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
